1
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.072
I’m Al Brooks.

2
00:00:03.072 --> 00:00:05.506
Thank you for watching the
Brooks Trading Course.

3
00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:11.245
This is the final video on
chart basics and price action.

4
00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:19.620
I will be talking about candlestick
patterns, I will talk about...

5
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.892
..what traders talk about, and finally
I will talk some about indicators.

6
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:33.954
I think one of the unfortunate
things that beginners see...

7
00:00:33.954 --> 00:00:39.126
..when they start out is a collection
of ads and claims on the Internet

8
00:00:39.126 --> 00:00:43.577
and in books and magazines that make
it sound like if you simply memorize...

9
00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:46.780
..a handful of candlestick patterns,
you’re going to get rich.

10
00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.921
And it’s really deceiving, because
there’s nothing easy in trading.

11
00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:57.744
You’re competing against the smartest
people in the world who are working...

12
00:00:57.744 --> 00:01:01.895
..extremely hard, and they are not
going to give up their money easily.

13
00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:06.927
So if you see ads like this
that tell you that you can make...

14
00:01:06.928 --> 00:01:11.058
..an incredible amount of money with
minimum work – where for example,

15
00:01:11.058 --> 00:01:17.044
this one says you can turn $250 into
$34,000 completely on autopilot.

16
00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.039
It’s really tempting.

17
00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:21.488
Everyone starting out is
looking for protection.

18
00:01:21.488 --> 00:01:23.750
They’re afraid of losing their money.

19
00:01:24.491 --> 00:01:26.887
They’re looking for someone who’s
going to take care of them.

20
00:01:26.887 --> 00:01:28.589
But nobody’s going to
take care of them.

21
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.159
They’re looking for some
easy way to make money...

22
00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.862
..that’s guaranteed to not lose money.

23
00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:40.414
And all of the ads imply that
all you have to do is memorize...

24
00:01:40.414 --> 00:01:43.730
..a few candlestick patterns and
they’ll work all the time,

25
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:47.174
or they’ll work 90% of the
time, and you’ll soon be rich...

26
00:01:47.174 --> 00:01:50.044
..like everybody else,
like Warren Buffett.

27
00:01:50.044 --> 00:01:52.052
But that’s not real,
it’s just not real.

28
00:01:52.052 --> 00:01:53.380
It’s misleading.

29
00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.690
So whenever you see anything
like this, just ignore it.

30
00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:58.185
Move on to something else.

31
00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:04.458
Now you correctly believe that there are
institutions that make a lot of money.

32
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:10.430
There are high frequency trading firms
(HFT firms), hedge funds, Goldman Sachs.

33
00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.867
Most of the firms out there
making a lot of money...

34
00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.870
..are not making them based
upon candlestick patterns.

35
00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:20.974
And if candlestick patterns
were the key to wealth,

36
00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:23.717
everyone would be using
them to make money.

37
00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:25.012
But that’s not the reality.

38
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.817
Lots of successful day traders
talk about their trades.

39
00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:35.322
For example, if you watch Fast
Money, the television show on CNBC,

40
00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:38.592
you’ll listen to the traders
talk constantly about trends,

41
00:02:38.592 --> 00:02:43.664
channels, prior highs, prior
lows, support and resistance.

42
00:02:43.664 --> 00:02:48.068
And you’ll never hear them say anything
about a particular candlestick pattern.

43
00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.904
Like “Oh I sold because
of a dark cloud cover...

44
00:02:50.905 --> 00:02:53.574
..or shooting star or Harami pattern.”

45
00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:58.785
They don’t talk about that
because that is such a tiny part...

46
00:02:58.785 --> 00:03:02.249
..of trading that it’s not
going to make you any money.

47
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.385
You have to learn far more
than that to be successful.

48
00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:08.449
Now look at this.

49
00:03:08.449 --> 00:03:10.257
Here’s a candlestick bottom.

50
00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:14.695
The market’s going down, tries to
bottom, tries to bottom again.

51
00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:18.198
Can you make money from this candlestick
pattern? Of course you can.

52
00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:21.515
The way to do it is you don’t buy.

53
00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:22.903
You wait for a few bars.

54
00:03:25.072 --> 00:03:28.975
Then you sell where the
bulls will get out.

55
00:03:29.669 --> 00:03:31.538
The bulls are trying to buy a bottom.

56
00:03:31.538 --> 00:03:35.515
Trends are resistant to change;
they’re probably going to continue.

57
00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:39.686
The bulls who buy here are going
to get trapped and lose money,

58
00:03:39.687 --> 00:03:42.469
so rather than buy here, look to sell...

59
00:03:42.469 --> 00:03:44.758
..where they’ll get out,
where they’ll get stopped out.

60
00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:48.904
So yes, you can make money trading a
candlestick pattern doing the opposite...

61
00:03:48.904 --> 00:03:53.667
..of what conventional candlestick
pattern teaches you to do.

62
00:03:55.936 --> 00:03:56.870
Look at this.

63
00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.973
Here we have a bearish engulfing
top on the daily chart.

64
00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.005
The textbooks would tell you, “Ah,
this bar traded above the high...

65
00:04:05.005 --> 00:04:07.267
..of that bar and then
it closed on its low,

66
00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:12.519
and it’s a big bear bar closing on its
low – it’s a short. It’s a short.”

67
00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.896
Well, the risk is not all that great.

68
00:04:15.896 --> 00:04:16.657
It’s to this point.

69
00:04:16.657 --> 00:04:18.946
The reward, maybe we come
all the way down here.

70
00:04:18.946 --> 00:04:19.887
That’s good too.

71
00:04:19.887 --> 00:04:21.595
So, great risk/reward.

72
00:04:21.962 --> 00:04:28.068
However, what about probability?
80% of reversal attempts fail.

73
00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:32.246
So this failed, this failed, this
failed, this failed, this failed.

74
00:04:32.246 --> 00:04:33.173
Failed.

75
00:04:33.874 --> 00:04:38.345
This one looks better than the others,
but is it going to succeed?

76
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:43.049
No. Whenever you see a top,
you have to expect...

77
00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:46.053
..that the top will fail
and become a bull flag.

78
00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.189
Don’t be too quick to sell a top.

79
00:04:49.189 --> 00:04:54.561
Instead, you have a better chance of
making money if you wait a few bars

80
00:04:54.561 --> 00:04:59.666
for the top to fail and become a bull flag
and then buy as the trend resumes up.

81
00:05:01.735 --> 00:05:02.636
Look at this.

82
00:05:02.636 --> 00:05:05.272
Here we have a bullish engulfing bar.

83
00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:07.541
It traded below the lows
of all of these bars...

84
00:05:07.541 --> 00:05:10.243
..and then reversed up strongly
and closed on its high.

85
00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.479
But you need context.

86
00:05:13.213 --> 00:05:16.616
Context means you have to look
at all the bars to the left,

87
00:05:16.617 --> 00:05:18.385
and they have to support your trade.

88
00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.454
Now look at these bars to the left.

89
00:05:21.848 --> 00:05:27.394
A very Tight Bear Channel with very little
in terms of pullbacks along the way.

90
00:05:28.028 --> 00:05:31.818
What is the probability that
the first reversal up is going...

91
00:05:31.818 --> 00:05:35.502
..to lead to a bull trend? The
probability is very low,

92
00:05:35.503 --> 00:05:38.505
yet you have a great-looking
candlestick pattern.

93
00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.975
But the candlestick pattern
alone is not enough.

94
00:05:41.975 --> 00:05:47.874
It has to be in a context that makes
sense, and this does not make sense.

95
00:05:47.874 --> 00:05:49.649
This is a low probability trade.

96
00:05:50.584 --> 00:05:55.222
So what do you do? Well, you know
the candlestick guys are buying,

97
00:05:55.223 --> 00:05:59.399
betting on the trend reversal,
but the smart guys are saying...

98
00:05:59.399 --> 00:06:03.563
..“Ah, this is a pullback in a bear
trend, and therefore it’ll fail...

99
00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:08.134
..and become a bear flag.” What
they do is they don’t buy here;

100
00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:11.705
they place a sell stop to go short
below the bear bar that followed it,

101
00:06:12.773 --> 00:06:16.710
betting that, like most
reversals, this one will fail...

102
00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.812
..and the bear trend will continue.

103
00:06:24.151 --> 00:06:26.353
Markets have inertia.

104
00:06:26.354 --> 00:06:31.738
That means they are resistant to
change, and there’s an 80% chance...

105
00:06:31.738 --> 00:06:34.961
..that they’ll continue doing
what they have been doing.

106
00:06:35.214 --> 00:06:39.646
So for example, if you want to know
what the bars to the right look like,

107
00:06:39.646 --> 00:06:42.529
the ones that you don’t see
yet, look to the left.

108
00:06:42.529 --> 00:06:46.039
If we’re in a bear trend, chances are
we’re going to continue in a bear trend.

109
00:06:47.641 --> 00:06:51.011
If we’re in a Trading Range, chances
are we’ll continue in a Trading Range.

110
00:06:51.011 --> 00:06:54.347
There’s much more to a bottom than
simply a candlestick pattern.

111
00:06:55.715 --> 00:07:01.188
So if you’re in a bear trend, you make
more money expecting reversals to fail.

112
00:07:01.189 --> 00:07:04.758
Y’know we had lots of reversals
here – here, here, here.

113
00:07:05.659 --> 00:07:10.463
We tried to reverse here and here, here
– most reversals are going to fail.

114
00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:15.202
Every one of those reversals is minor.

115
00:07:15.203 --> 00:07:17.704
They are not Major Trend Reversals.

116
00:07:17.704 --> 00:07:21.541
They are not going to change a
bear trend into a bull trend.

117
00:07:21.542 --> 00:07:24.811
They’re going to change a
bear trend into a bear flag,

118
00:07:24.812 --> 00:07:29.249
and then the bear flag will lead
to a resumption of the bear trend.

119
00:07:32.066 --> 00:07:34.636
My 80% rule, inertia.

120
00:07:35.408 --> 00:07:39.546
When the market’s in a trend, 80%
of reversal attempts will fail.

121
00:07:40.538 --> 00:07:43.677
They’re minor reversals and
they become bear flags,

122
00:07:43.677 --> 00:07:46.494
and they lead to resumption
of the trend down.

123
00:07:46.495 --> 00:07:48.937
So for example, here we’re
trying to reverse up.

124
00:07:48.937 --> 00:07:50.385
We have a small Double Bottom.

125
00:07:50.906 --> 00:07:53.012
Am I going to buy that bar? No.

126
00:07:53.013 --> 00:07:56.241
If anything, I’m going to place a limit
order to sell the high of the bar.

127
00:07:56.241 --> 00:07:57.140
Same here.

128
00:07:57.704 --> 00:07:59.565
Here’s a bull bar closing on its high.

129
00:07:59.565 --> 00:08:01.833
Am I going to buy that close? No.

130
00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:05.732
If anything, I’m going to place a
market order to sell as soon as I see...

131
00:08:05.732 --> 00:08:09.662
..that big bull bar attempting to
reverse up, because I know the math...

132
00:08:09.662 --> 00:08:12.927
..is it’s more likely to
lead to resumption down.

133
00:08:12.928 --> 00:08:14.283
And that’s true all the way down.

134
00:08:14.283 --> 00:08:16.021
Every one of the reversal attempts,

135
00:08:16.021 --> 00:08:19.648
I’m viewing as a bear flag,
and I’m looking to sell.

136
00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:24.530
Bulls finally got their bounce.

137
00:08:25.032 --> 00:08:28.155
The bulls who have been buying all
the way down finally made money,

138
00:08:28.155 --> 00:08:31.613
but they lost money on all
the other prior attempts.

139
00:08:31.613 --> 00:08:35.007
And what they make here
will probably not be enough...

140
00:08:35.007 --> 00:08:36.695
..to offset their prior losses.

141
00:08:36.696 --> 00:08:39.553
And even this is only a minor reversal.

142
00:08:39.554 --> 00:08:43.096
When the channel is this tight, you
might bounce for 10 or 20 bars,

143
00:08:43.096 --> 00:08:46.324
but the odds are you’re going to
come back down and test this low.

144
00:08:46.598 --> 00:08:49.506
At that point you might
get a major reversal,

145
00:08:49.507 --> 00:08:53.376
but all these reversals, including
this one, is probably minor.

146
00:08:55.796 --> 00:08:59.372
Now, my 80% rule also
applies to Trading Ranges.

147
00:09:00.418 --> 00:09:03.486
In a trend, 80% of
reversal attempts fail.

148
00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:09.498
In a Trading Range, 80% of attempts
to break out into a trend will fail.

149
00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:15.060
So we tried to go to a new
high but reversed down.

150
00:09:15.061 --> 00:09:16.668
A new low, reversed up.

151
00:09:16.668 --> 00:09:17.938
New low, reversed up.

152
00:09:17.938 --> 00:09:19.399
New high, reversed down.

153
00:09:19.399 --> 00:09:21.121
New low, reversed up.

154
00:09:21.121 --> 00:09:22.841
New high, reversed down.

155
00:09:24.487 --> 00:09:27.675
If you see a market having a lot
of Trading Range price action,

156
00:09:27.676 --> 00:09:30.409
don’t get excited when it
breaks to the downside.

157
00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:34.896
You have to assume the
downside breakout will fail.

158
00:09:34.897 --> 00:09:37.457
And don’t get excited when
it breaks to the upside.

159
00:09:37.881 --> 00:09:40.598
Even when it’s breaking strongly
to the upside like this,

160
00:09:40.598 --> 00:09:44.924
the odds are that it will fail,
at least pull back a little.

161
00:09:44.924 --> 00:09:47.007
Here it pulled back all
the way to a new low.

162
00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.276
Trading is difficult to do.

163
00:09:53.276 --> 00:09:55.549
I’ve been trading for 30 years,
and it’s still difficult,

164
00:09:55.549 --> 00:09:59.170
but I enjoy doing it and I’m
very peaceful when I do it.

165
00:09:59.402 --> 00:10:03.009
When traders start out, they quickly
learn that they lose money.

166
00:10:03.009 --> 00:10:08.157
No matter how hard they try to trade
really well, no matter how much...

167
00:10:08.157 --> 00:10:11.005
..they know about candlestick
patterns, they’re losing money.

168
00:10:11.005 --> 00:10:12.848
So they realize they’re
missing something.

169
00:10:13.354 --> 00:10:14.826
For example, here.

170
00:10:15.052 --> 00:10:18.070
A sell, a sell, but the
market keeps going up.

171
00:10:20.166 --> 00:10:23.030
What they’re missing is
understanding context.

172
00:10:23.031 --> 00:10:25.974
Context means all of
the bars to the left.

173
00:10:25.975 --> 00:10:29.761
And what the market has been
doing prior to the current bar

174
00:10:29.761 --> 00:10:33.718
is far more important than what
the current bar looks like.

175
00:10:34.649 --> 00:10:37.295
Candlestick patterns alone are useless.

176
00:10:37.295 --> 00:10:39.988
If anything, when you’re
starting out, you’ll lose money...

177
00:10:39.988 --> 00:10:45.132
..because you’ll constantly be
betting that trends will reverse

178
00:10:45.133 --> 00:10:49.360
and you’ll constantly be betting
that Trading Ranges will break out –

179
00:10:49.361 --> 00:10:52.144
and 80% of the time, you’re wrong.

180
00:10:52.442 --> 00:10:56.386
You’re taking 20% best, and
it’s virtually impossible...

181
00:10:56.386 --> 00:10:59.392
..to be making money if you
win only 20% of the time.

182
00:11:02.059 --> 00:11:05.807
After traders lose enough money,
they start to look for help.

183
00:11:05.807 --> 00:11:07.986
They’re desperate to
believe in anything.

184
00:11:07.986 --> 00:11:11.566
And there are lots of
well-intentioned people out there...

185
00:11:11.566 --> 00:11:15.094
..who want to help you, but a
lot of them are dishonest,

186
00:11:15.095 --> 00:11:19.798
and a lot of them teach you that
knowing candlestick patterns...

187
00:11:19.799 --> 00:11:23.476
..is the only road to making
a fortune as a trader.

188
00:11:24.018 --> 00:11:25.702
And that’s simply not the case.

189
00:11:25.703 --> 00:11:27.506
Here, big bull reversal bar.

190
00:11:27.506 --> 00:11:29.193
Buy? No, you don’t buy.

191
00:11:29.194 --> 00:11:30.562
It’s following 3 bear bars.

192
00:11:30.562 --> 00:11:31.734
Look to the left.

193
00:11:31.734 --> 00:11:34.986
The market’s going down, so if
anything, you’re looking to sell.

194
00:11:37.274 --> 00:11:41.084
So if candlesticks are not the
answer, then what is price action?

195
00:11:41.368 --> 00:11:43.333
Listen to the traders on television,

196
00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:45.612
expert traders, traders
who trade for a living.

197
00:11:46.087 --> 00:11:47.230
Listen to what they say.

198
00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.148
They tell you every
day what’s important,

199
00:11:49.149 --> 00:11:52.443
and they virtually never
mention a candlestick pattern.

200
00:11:54.048 --> 00:11:56.643
So what do traders talk about?
If they’re not talking...

201
00:11:56.643 --> 00:11:59.754
..about all these candlestick patterns
that you see on the Internet,

202
00:11:59.755 --> 00:12:02.446
what are they talking about?
How are they making money?

203
00:12:04.878 --> 00:12:09.482
One of the most important things that they
talk about is support and resistance.

204
00:12:09.764 --> 00:12:11.827
And that comes in many forms.

205
00:12:12.133 --> 00:12:13.490
Moving Averages.

206
00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:14.606
Channels.

207
00:12:15.194 --> 00:12:17.974
Here’s the average price, right?
They’re interested to see...

208
00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:20.383
..how the market reacts
to the average price.

209
00:12:20.383 --> 00:12:23.832
So we’re falling down strongly,
and when it gets back...

210
00:12:23.832 --> 00:12:26.616
..to the average price,
that’s probably expensive.

211
00:12:26.616 --> 00:12:28.059
Traders will look to sell.

212
00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.622
It becomes resistance.

213
00:12:30.974 --> 00:12:32.840
Here, we’re rallying strongly.

214
00:12:32.841 --> 00:12:35.083
When it gets down near
the average price...

215
00:12:35.083 --> 00:12:38.431
..over the past 20 bars, 100
bars, it reverses up.

216
00:12:38.633 --> 00:12:39.733
Support.

217
00:12:39.733 --> 00:12:41.191
And they also look at channels.

218
00:12:41.191 --> 00:12:46.720
Here’s a bear channel after a bull
breakout, so it’s probably a bull flag.

219
00:12:48.118 --> 00:12:51.620
Traders also spend a lot of time
looking at prior highs and lows.

220
00:12:52.876 --> 00:12:55.402
The market rallied to
this point and sold off.

221
00:12:55.944 --> 00:13:01.453
It broke strongly above it, came down
near that point, and it’s now support.

222
00:13:01.453 --> 00:13:02.831
It rallied again.

223
00:13:02.831 --> 00:13:05.604
It broke below it, tried to
get above it again, failed.

224
00:13:05.604 --> 00:13:07.533
Tried to get above it again, failed.

225
00:13:07.534 --> 00:13:13.061
That high was resistance, and then
support, and then resistance again.

226
00:13:13.061 --> 00:13:15.832
This low, the market broke
strongly low below it.

227
00:13:15.832 --> 00:13:17.622
It tested it, could not get above it.

228
00:13:17.622 --> 00:13:18.616
There was resistance.

229
00:13:18.616 --> 00:13:20.612
Tried to get above it
again, resistance.

230
00:13:20.612 --> 00:13:22.781
Tried to get above it
again, resistance.

231
00:13:25.326 --> 00:13:30.065
Another thing that traders always
talk about is how strong a trend is.

232
00:13:30.338 --> 00:13:35.481
For example, if the market’s in a bull
trend, you want to see Higher Lows.

233
00:13:36.112 --> 00:13:38.088
You want to see Higher Highs.

234
00:13:38.088 --> 00:13:43.979
And if you see that, traders are more
inclined to buy – buy for any reason.

235
00:13:44.661 --> 00:13:50.286
In a bear trend, they look at Lower
Highs and they want to see Lower Lows.

236
00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.323
And if the market is going
down, they’re more inclined...

237
00:13:52.323 --> 00:13:55.089
..to sell until there’s
a clear reversal up.

238
00:13:55.089 --> 00:13:58.617
Here, a bear trend,
strong bull breakout.

239
00:13:58.618 --> 00:14:02.761
Higher Low, big enough pattern
for a Major Trend Reversal,

240
00:14:02.762 --> 00:14:04.704
and it reversed into a bull trend.

241
00:14:09.199 --> 00:14:11.201
Bear channel, bear trend.

242
00:14:11.201 --> 00:14:13.331
Bull channel, bull trend.

243
00:14:17.186 --> 00:14:21.829
There are two forces that are very
important, and they control all markets.

244
00:14:21.829 --> 00:14:24.104
First of all there’s
context, and momentum.

245
00:14:25.378 --> 00:14:29.278
Remember I said that context
means all the bars to the left.

246
00:14:29.279 --> 00:14:32.873
Where is the support and resistance?
I talk about this...

247
00:14:32.873 --> 00:14:35.761
..in a separate video on
support and resistance.

248
00:14:38.019 --> 00:14:42.985
For example, we’re falling here, and
if you draw a line across these tops,

249
00:14:42.999 --> 00:14:46.088
you’ll see that every time it
gets near the line, it falls.

250
00:14:46.088 --> 00:14:49.110
Even if it gets above the line, it
falls – above the line, it falls.

251
00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:53.653
And prior highs and lows are important.

252
00:14:53.653 --> 00:14:56.064
We’re in a bear trend;
you’re looking to sell.

253
00:14:56.064 --> 00:15:00.084
Selling pullbacks is a good thing to
do, so if it gets near a trend line...

254
00:15:00.084 --> 00:15:02.898
..and reverses down, that’s
a good thing to sell.

255
00:15:02.898 --> 00:15:04.552
Near the trend line, reverses down.

256
00:15:04.552 --> 00:15:09.833
Near the trend line, place a stop order
to go short just below the prior bar.

257
00:15:10.943 --> 00:15:12.185
Then look at this.

258
00:15:12.541 --> 00:15:15.447
Every time it gets near the
prior low, it goes up.

259
00:15:15.948 --> 00:15:18.177
So there’s support at prior lows.

260
00:15:18.689 --> 00:15:21.091
Traders will look to buy reversals up.

261
00:15:21.389 --> 00:15:25.281
When the market makes a new
low, they’ll place a stop order...

262
00:15:25.282 --> 00:15:26.963
..to buy above the high of the prior bar.

263
00:15:26.964 --> 00:15:29.268
These little green boxes
are where they get in.

264
00:15:35.764 --> 00:15:43.142
Traders who look to sell at resistance
and buy at support are value investors.

265
00:15:43.638 --> 00:15:47.514
They want to buy when it’s cheap
and sell when it’s expensive.

266
00:15:50.514 --> 00:15:52.328
Now, I said there were two things.

267
00:15:52.328 --> 00:15:54.278
I said context and momentum.

268
00:15:55.682 --> 00:15:58.111
Momentum refers to the
strength of the trend.

269
00:15:58.111 --> 00:16:02.853
The video on breakouts talks
a lot more about momentum.

270
00:16:03.142 --> 00:16:04.165
Now look at this.

271
00:16:04.165 --> 00:16:07.672
We’re falling pretty strongly here,
rallying pretty strongly here.

272
00:16:10.606 --> 00:16:15.217
When momentum is strong, traders want to
trade in the direction of the momentum.

273
00:16:15.217 --> 00:16:18.677
So if it’s falling strongly,
traders should be looking to sell.

274
00:16:18.678 --> 00:16:22.933
You can sell even the close of this
bar, betting that any reversal up...

275
00:16:22.934 --> 00:16:27.704
..will probably stay below that high
and be followed by lower prices.

276
00:16:28.193 --> 00:16:29.452
And the same is true here.

277
00:16:29.452 --> 00:16:30.952
You could buy the close of this bar,

278
00:16:30.953 --> 00:16:33.699
knowing that there’ll be at
least a little bit more up.

279
00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:37.350
And here, it pulled back
but held above the bottom...

280
00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.732
..of the bull trend, and it
starts to turn up again.

281
00:16:39.732 --> 00:16:42.181
So traders will buy on
the reversal back up.

282
00:16:44.464 --> 00:16:46.822
So they’ll buy the
breakout or the pullback.

283
00:16:46.823 --> 00:16:49.823
Here, they’ll sell the
breakout or the pullback.

284
00:16:49.824 --> 00:16:51.206
They don’t sell simply here.

285
00:16:51.206 --> 00:16:52.635
They sold all the way down.

286
00:16:52.635 --> 00:16:55.811
You could even sell at the
worst price and make money.

287
00:16:55.812 --> 00:16:57.125
The same with here.

288
00:16:57.125 --> 00:16:59.224
Traders don’t all buy that close.

289
00:16:59.224 --> 00:17:01.595
A lot of them bought
all the way up here.

290
00:17:01.595 --> 00:17:04.491
That’s why we got this strong
breakout; everybody’s buying.

291
00:17:08.019 --> 00:17:08.883
Look at here.

292
00:17:09.352 --> 00:17:10.781
The market’s losing momentum.

293
00:17:10.781 --> 00:17:13.509
We have a couple bear bars, but they’re
small, followed by a bull bar.

294
00:17:13.509 --> 00:17:14.803
A bear bar with a tail.

295
00:17:14.803 --> 00:17:17.673
A small bear bar followed
by a bull reversal bar.

296
00:17:19.266 --> 00:17:21.452
The momentum down is getting weak.

297
00:17:21.452 --> 00:17:23.777
Compare that to this.

298
00:17:24.972 --> 00:17:26.693
Traders are buying every low.

299
00:17:26.976 --> 00:17:29.867
Bulls are making money
buying every low,

300
00:17:29.867 --> 00:17:32.413
betting that the trend will
not fall that much further.

301
00:17:32.931 --> 00:17:39.067
The market is transitioning from a strong
bear trend into a weak bear trend,

302
00:17:39.067 --> 00:17:41.391
and then possibly a Trading Range
Double Bottom)...

303
00:17:41.391 --> 00:17:44.125
..and then possibly even a bull trend.

304
00:17:44.652 --> 00:17:49.652
So the momentum is weakening and traders
start looking for reversal trades.

305
00:17:50.584 --> 00:17:52.593
For example, buy the reversal up.

306
00:17:52.593 --> 00:17:56.245
We have a Double Bottom, maybe a
slightly Lower Low Major Trend Reversal.

307
00:17:56.631 --> 00:17:59.982
We have a bear trend, strong
bull breakout above the top...

308
00:17:59.982 --> 00:18:04.366
..of the bear channel, and then
a test of the bear trend low

309
00:18:04.366 --> 00:18:07.790
and a reversal up, and a second
and a third reversal up.

310
00:18:08.527 --> 00:18:12.103
So that is a reasonable
reversal trade to take.

311
00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:17.875
I pay a lot of attention to
early signs of strength.

312
00:18:18.113 --> 00:18:21.042
So we’re in a bear
trend, but look at this.

313
00:18:21.042 --> 00:18:24.204
We have 4 consecutive
bull bars, 2 of them...

314
00:18:24.204 --> 00:18:27.815
..with very big bull bodies, all
4 closing near their highs.

315
00:18:28.183 --> 00:18:32.856
Bear trend, yes, but we have
a sudden burst of buying.

316
00:18:32.856 --> 00:18:36.009
And, that’s a lot of strength
on the part of the bulls,

317
00:18:36.009 --> 00:18:38.331
and they refer to that
as Buying Pressure.

318
00:18:38.627 --> 00:18:41.241
So I pay attention to Buying Pressure.

319
00:18:41.242 --> 00:18:45.552
Here, here, we sold off strongly
but it reversed up strongly.

320
00:18:46.439 --> 00:18:48.622
The market is becoming more bullish.

321
00:18:48.622 --> 00:18:50.468
We’re getting a lot of Buying Pressure.

322
00:18:51.494 --> 00:18:53.431
And on the way down,
I look at Selling Pressure.

323
00:18:53.431 --> 00:18:55.277
We have a lot of bars down.

324
00:18:55.278 --> 00:18:59.938
Every bar, the high is below the high
of the prior bar; the low is below...

325
00:18:59.938 --> 00:19:03.565
..the low of the prior bar, so we’re
trending down pretty strongly.

326
00:19:03.565 --> 00:19:08.116
Odds are selling for any reason, we’ll
get at least a little bit more down.

327
00:19:10.189 --> 00:19:13.199
Traders also pay attention to
the strength of the trend.

328
00:19:13.199 --> 00:19:16.771
I told you that in addition
to risk and reward,

329
00:19:16.771 --> 00:19:18.941
they need to pay attention
to probability.

330
00:19:18.942 --> 00:19:21.945
And a very important thing
is trade management.

331
00:19:21.946 --> 00:19:25.149
Once they take a trade, they
have to manage it correctly.

332
00:19:28.299 --> 00:19:33.827
To make money as a trader, candlestick
patterns that’s not the answer.

333
00:19:34.101 --> 00:19:36.647
They’re basically totally unnecessary.

334
00:19:36.648 --> 00:19:40.906
They can be a useful small
piece of the big picture,

335
00:19:40.906 --> 00:19:42.495
but they’re really not important.

336
00:19:42.495 --> 00:19:45.576
A lot of institutions
trade off line charts.

337
00:19:45.903 --> 00:19:47.607
They don’t care about the
candlestick patterns.

338
00:19:47.607 --> 00:19:50.639
They know that the direction of the
trend, the strength of the trend,

339
00:19:50.639 --> 00:19:54.250
support and resistance are far more
important than candlestick patterns.

340
00:19:55.395 --> 00:19:59.417
So if you look at this line
chart, are you thinking...

341
00:19:59.417 --> 00:20:02.035
..that a candlestick pattern
would make it more bullish?

342
00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:04.064
Or are you saying “Wow, this
is going up really fast.

343
00:20:04.064 --> 00:20:06.850
Higher Lows, Higher Highs
– I’ve got to buy”?

344
00:20:07.708 --> 00:20:10.661
A candlestick pattern is not going
to make it any more bullish.

345
00:20:10.661 --> 00:20:12.538
When you see this, you’ve got to buy,

346
00:20:12.538 --> 00:20:14.846
and the candlestick pattern
will not help you.

347
00:20:18.205 --> 00:20:20.725
Now, I want to say a few
things about indicators.

348
00:20:21.846 --> 00:20:24.850
When I first started
trading, all the magazines...

349
00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:26.628
..had pictures that looked like this.

350
00:20:27.123 --> 00:20:31.309
They tried to stuff as many
indicators onto the chart as possible...

351
00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:34.152
..to lead you to believe that
if you buy their software...

352
00:20:34.152 --> 00:20:37.051
..that can create all of these
indicators, you’re going to get rich.

353
00:20:37.051 --> 00:20:41.041
You’ll have some big advantages
that will allow you to make money.

354
00:20:42.565 --> 00:20:44.897
Does all of this stuff really help?

355
00:20:45.274 --> 00:20:48.958
If one indicator is good,
is two, three, four better?

356
00:20:48.958 --> 00:20:50.784
Having 10, is that better?

357
00:20:53.083 --> 00:20:54.430
The answer is no.

358
00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.021
In fact, you can barely see the chart

359
00:20:57.021 --> 00:20:59.349
with all of these indicators
all over the chart.

360
00:20:59.349 --> 00:21:03.172
Your eye is going to get
focused onto the indicators...

361
00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.982
..and you will not be paying
attention to the chart.

362
00:21:07.209 --> 00:21:09.925
Here’s the same chart with
the indicators removed.

363
00:21:09.926 --> 00:21:11.641
I can see what’s going on.

364
00:21:11.641 --> 00:21:13.447
The bulls are trying to break out.

365
00:21:13.447 --> 00:21:15.321
We have a big reversal bar.

366
00:21:15.321 --> 00:21:17.477
We’re probably going
to continue back down.

367
00:21:17.478 --> 00:21:19.741
A Trading Range breakout
probably will fail.

368
00:21:21.339 --> 00:21:22.282
I’m looking to sell.

369
00:21:22.845 --> 00:21:26.619
Three pushes down, a Trading Range
breakout below – I’m looking to buy.

370
00:21:31.236 --> 00:21:34.465
A Triangle, breakout,
small Triangle inside...

371
00:21:34.465 --> 00:21:37.264
..of a bigger Triangle –
I’m probably going to sell.

372
00:21:39.794 --> 00:21:42.532
Strong bear trend, a bull reversal,

373
00:21:42.532 --> 00:21:44.830
probably going to fail
– I’m looking to sell.

374
00:21:45.374 --> 00:21:48.687
A minor reversal, possible Final Flag,

375
00:21:48.688 --> 00:21:51.905
decent buy reversal bar
– I’ll look to buy.

376
00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:58.482
50% pullback from the selloff, I’m
going to start looking to sell.

377
00:21:58.885 --> 00:22:00.874
Ok, we’ve got a second entry short,

378
00:22:00.874 --> 00:22:04.068
we have a small Double Top
here, I’m looking to sell.

379
00:22:06.925 --> 00:22:09.468
Small Triangle, failed bull breakout.

380
00:22:09.799 --> 00:22:12.701
I’m going to bet that will continue
down at least for a little bit more.

381
00:22:12.701 --> 00:22:13.850
I’m looking to sell.

382
00:22:14.662 --> 00:22:17.287
Higher Low Major Trend Reversal.

383
00:22:17.288 --> 00:22:21.131
Bear trend, bull breakout, Higher
Low, but selloff not all that strong.

384
00:22:21.131 --> 00:22:25.263
Two legs down – one, pullback,
two – I’m going to look to buy.

385
00:22:25.263 --> 00:22:27.764
And the indicators don’t
show me any of that.

386
00:22:28.541 --> 00:22:33.691
So for me, I personally prefer just to
look at the charts and try to understand...

387
00:22:33.691 --> 00:22:38.169
..what the market is doing, and then
I place trades based upon the price action.

388
00:22:38.169 --> 00:22:42.019
To me, I don’t like indicators because
I get stressed out constantly looking...

389
00:22:42.019 --> 00:22:47.445
..for reversals in trends and constantly
looking for breakouts in Trading Ranges.

390
00:22:47.445 --> 00:22:50.129
And it’s the exact opposite
of what I should be doing.

391
00:22:51.527 --> 00:22:53.418
This is a common thing that you see.

392
00:22:53.419 --> 00:22:58.709
Ok, look at this low and
this low in the indicator.

393
00:22:58.709 --> 00:23:02.381
So we’ve got a low, we have a
Higher Low, we have a Higher Low.

394
00:23:02.381 --> 00:23:04.945
This is a divergence, this
is a double divergence.

395
00:23:05.514 --> 00:23:07.462
And the websites will
tell you, “Ah, you’ve got...

396
00:23:07.462 --> 00:23:10.060
..a double divergence,
you’ve got to look to buy.

397
00:23:11.474 --> 00:23:17.904
Right? Here we’ve got lower prices and
then we have a higher oscillator.

398
00:23:17.904 --> 00:23:19.255
You have to buy.”

399
00:23:19.255 --> 00:23:21.186
No. Look at the bars.

400
00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:27.146
You’re in a really Tight Bear Channel
with virtually no significant pullback.

401
00:23:27.146 --> 00:23:29.529
It’s far easier to make money selling.

402
00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:33.166
So even though we’ve got a divergence
– here’s another divergence –

403
00:23:34.570 --> 00:23:37.696
price is going down,
indicator is going up.

404
00:23:37.696 --> 00:23:38.622
Higher Lows.

405
00:23:39.134 --> 00:23:42.576
It’s crazy, right?
That’s the single biggest problem...

406
00:23:42.576 --> 00:23:44.388
..with indicators for beginners.

407
00:23:44.389 --> 00:23:47.806
They look at the indicator or patterns.

408
00:23:47.807 --> 00:23:49.108
“Oh, a diversion.

409
00:23:49.108 --> 00:23:51.516
I’ve got to buy.”
They don’t look at the chart.

410
00:23:52.078 --> 00:23:54.727
When the market’s in a
Small Pullback Bear Trend,

411
00:23:54.727 --> 00:23:57.374
you can only make money
selling, not buying.

412
00:24:00.892 --> 00:24:04.912
So indicators, it’s an excuse to
avoid thinking about the obvious.

413
00:24:04.912 --> 00:24:10.891
So buying in a strong bear trend – yes,
it can work and you can make a fortune.

414
00:24:10.892 --> 00:24:13.062
But, so the risk/reward is great.

415
00:24:13.062 --> 00:24:15.826
You buy here, your risk is here.

416
00:24:15.827 --> 00:24:17.520
Very little money at risk.

417
00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:20.585
We could go up forever,
so your reward is huge.

418
00:24:20.586 --> 00:24:25.840
However, what is the probability?
The probability is extremely low.

419
00:24:25.841 --> 00:24:28.458
So you need much more than risk/reward.

420
00:24:28.459 --> 00:24:30.465
One of the unfortunate
things on television...

421
00:24:30.465 --> 00:24:33.901
..is traders constantly talk
about risk and reward.

422
00:24:33.901 --> 00:24:38.319
They never talk about probability, but
that’s the flipside of risk/reward.

423
00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:41.979
Whenever a trade has
excellent risk/reward...

424
00:24:41.979 --> 00:24:47.195
..(in other words, small risk, great reward)
it also has very little probability.

425
00:24:47.195 --> 00:24:51.168
Because there has to be a reason for
an institution to take the other side.

426
00:24:51.168 --> 00:24:55.977
So if you get great risk/reward,
guess what? The institution taking...

427
00:24:55.977 --> 00:24:58.637
..the other side of your trade
has high probability.

428
00:24:58.638 --> 00:25:00.577
He’s probably going to make money.

429
00:25:00.577 --> 00:25:02.837
Every now and then you’ll
make a lot of money,

430
00:25:03.657 --> 00:25:05.913
but most of the time
you’re going to lose.

431
00:25:05.914 --> 00:25:08.211
So you keep getting these small losses.

432
00:25:08.212 --> 00:25:10.001
Your indicators are telling you to buy.

433
00:25:10.001 --> 00:25:11.759
Buy, buy, buy. Buy, buy, buy.

434
00:25:11.759 --> 00:25:12.668
You buy, you lose.

435
00:25:12.668 --> 00:25:13.495
You buy, you lose.

436
00:25:13.495 --> 00:25:14.781
You buy, you lose.

437
00:25:15.094 --> 00:25:17.885
And you’re not losing much –
remember, your risk is small –

438
00:25:17.885 --> 00:25:21.428
however, you can bleed to death
from a thousand papercuts.

439
00:25:21.429 --> 00:25:24.024
Those small losses add up.

440
00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:28.608
You have to be patient.

441
00:25:28.609 --> 00:25:29.819
There’s a lot to learn.

442
00:25:29.819 --> 00:25:32.257
That’s why there are so
many videos in this course.

443
00:25:32.258 --> 00:25:33.851
I’m trying to teach you everything...

444
00:25:33.851 --> 00:25:37.189
..that you need to know to
be a successful trader.

445
00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:39.546
And there are no shortcuts.

446
00:25:39.546 --> 00:25:41.567
Indicators are not a shortcut.

447
00:25:41.862 --> 00:25:44.397
Candlestick patterns are not a shortcut.

448
00:25:44.398 --> 00:25:48.243
And trading is never going to be easy
because you’re competing against...

449
00:25:48.243 --> 00:25:52.714
..extremely smart, hardworking people
who have been doing this for years,

450
00:25:52.714 --> 00:25:54.854
and they don’t want
to give you a penny.

451
00:25:54.855 --> 00:25:57.767
They want to take every penny that
they can get – and that’s their job.

452
00:25:57.767 --> 00:25:58.622
That’s what they should do.

453
00:25:58.622 --> 00:26:01.162
That’s my job, and that’s
what I try to do every day.

454
00:26:01.688 --> 00:26:05.722
But even though it’s hard, I
really enjoy the challenge.

455
00:26:07.508 --> 00:26:10.864
Well, what type of chart?
Look at this chart.

456
00:26:10.864 --> 00:26:12.516
Ok, this is the euro versus the yen.

457
00:26:12.516 --> 00:26:14.009
It’s a monthly chart.

458
00:26:14.809 --> 00:26:18.039
When you look at it, if you
didn’t look at the time axis,

459
00:26:18.039 --> 00:26:20.321
you would say maybe
it’s a 5-minute chart,

460
00:26:20.321 --> 00:26:22.725
maybe it’s a 1-minute chart,
maybe it’s a 60-minute chart.

461
00:26:22.725 --> 00:26:23.984
It’s a monthly chart.

462
00:26:24.494 --> 00:26:29.453
And the point I’m trying to make is some
traders do not want to trade intraday.

463
00:26:29.453 --> 00:26:32.965
And they’ll trade daily charts or
weekly charts or monthly charts.

464
00:26:32.966 --> 00:26:35.495
It doesn’t matter; the
process is still the same.

465
00:26:35.495 --> 00:26:37.009
The market’s going up.

466
00:26:37.009 --> 00:26:40.431
Traders are looking to buy pullbacks,
or they’ll even buy breakouts.

467
00:26:40.431 --> 00:26:44.249
If we’re trying to top,
traders will start to sell.

468
00:26:44.795 --> 00:26:46.489
This process is the same.

469
00:26:46.489 --> 00:26:48.757
It doesn’t matter what
the timeframe is.

470
00:26:48.757 --> 00:26:50.323
All markets are fractal.

471
00:26:50.882 --> 00:26:53.746
Bigger patterns are made
up of smaller patterns;

472
00:26:53.746 --> 00:26:56.490
smaller patterns are parts
of bigger patterns.

473
00:26:56.490 --> 00:26:57.930
It’s all the same thing.

474
00:27:02.945 --> 00:27:06.907
If you do trade a monthly
chart, the bars are very big,

475
00:27:06.908 --> 00:27:09.239
so the stop is very far away.

476
00:27:09.240 --> 00:27:13.302
You have to trade very small to make
sure that the risk on your trade...

477
00:27:13.302 --> 00:27:15.799
..is no bigger than the
risk on any other trade.

478
00:27:19.694 --> 00:27:22.170
In this video I talked about
candlestick patterns...

479
00:27:22.170 --> 00:27:25.005
..and how they are not
particularly helpful.

480
00:27:25.006 --> 00:27:29.222
I also discussed what
professional traders talk about.

481
00:27:29.222 --> 00:27:33.244
And as I said, they talk much more
about support and resistance,

482
00:27:33.245 --> 00:27:37.480
and momentum and strength of trends than
they do about candlestick patterns.

483
00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:40.056
They virtually never talk
about candlestick patterns.

484
00:27:40.057 --> 00:27:43.509
And I also talked about indicators
and how it’s very easy...

485
00:27:43.509 --> 00:27:45.555
..to get overly dependent on them.

486
00:27:45.556 --> 00:27:47.739
And if you use them, you’ll find...

487
00:27:47.739 --> 00:27:50.619
..that they probably don’t
help you make any money.

488
00:27:50.620 --> 00:27:53.523
I don’t have a problem with
somebody using indicators...

489
00:27:53.523 --> 00:27:56.290
..if they’re making money
and if they’re happy.

490
00:27:56.756 --> 00:28:01.082
But if you’re not making money and
if you’re stressed out using them,

491
00:28:01.082 --> 00:28:03.762
then I would get rid of them
and just look at the charts.

492
00:28:04.168 --> 00:28:07.692
And if you look on television,
you rarely ever see...

493
00:28:07.692 --> 00:28:09.544
..anybody putting an indicator up.

494
00:28:09.545 --> 00:28:13.666
And that’s because most professional
traders don’t pay attention to them.

495
00:28:13.667 --> 00:28:15.939
They pay attention to the price action.

496
00:28:19.773 --> 00:28:21.167
I’m Al Brooks.

497
00:28:21.167 --> 00:28:23.251
Thank you for watching the
Brooks Trading Course.

498
00:28:23.251 --> 00:28:27.673
This is the final video on
chart basics and price action.
